    <name>
      <text>Finding Inverses of Functions_9(i)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find  the inverse of the function \( \displaystyle f(x)={@func@}\)</p>
<p><b>Note:</b> \(\ln\) can be typed as <code> log</code></p>
<p>\(f^{-1}(x)=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To find the inverse of the function \( \displaystyle f(x)={@func@}\), express the function in terms of \(x\) and  \(y\) and proceed as follows</p>
<p> \(\begin{align}
\displaystyle f(x)&={@func@}\\
&x={@const*%e^(y^power)@}\\
&\displaystyle \frac{x}{{@const@}}={@%e^(y^power)@}\\
&{@sol3@}\\
\end{align}\)</p>
<p>Solving for \(y\) by finding  root  \({@power@}\) on both sides.</p>
<p>\(x={@sol4@}\)</p>
<p></p>
<p></p>
<p></p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
